    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I hear you on the 'intelligence' aspect, but I'm still feeling uneasy. \n\nIf we get halfway through the filing and the patent examiner comes back and says our \"adaptive modulation\" is actually just a logical extension of the \"pulse-modulated flow\" in 7720-C, we're in huge trouble. We'll have wasted months of dev time and tens of thousands in legal fees.\n\nCan you be brutally honest with me? On a scale of 1 to 10, how much of a risk is this patent actually? And if you were the examiner, what's the first thing you'd use to try and invalidate our claim? I need the unvarnished truth here, not just the optimistic version.",
